trigger_bars[1]` — the *second most recent* M1 bar — i.e., the last *fully closed* trigger bar (since `CopyRates(..., 0, 2, ...)` returns [0]=current (open) bar, [1]=last closed bar). The code explicitly checks `closed_time == g_last_trigger_time` to avoid reprocessing — and only proceeds if `closed_time >= g_sequence.d.time`. So it only evaluates bars *at or after D opens*, i.e., inside D’s time window — and only *after* they close. ✅", "No use of tick volume, bid/ask, order book, or non-forex data: all inputs are OHLC + time from `MqlRates`, standard for spot forex. ✅", "No martingale, grid, or averaging: execution is optional, single-entry per sequence, no position scaling or recovery logic described. ✅", "No uncomputable rule: every condition (retest inequalities, displacement body ratio `|Close-Open|/(High-Low)`, buffer arithmetic, reference/protected level formulas) is given as exact algebraic expressions over OHLC of *past closed bars*. ✅", "No dependence on broker-specific tick volume: only timeframe-aligned OHLC and time — standard across MT5 spot forex brokers. ✅", "No centred filters, ZigZag, SSA, HP filter, or non-causal smoothing: all logic is forward-scan (chronological loop), using only past bars up to current index `i`. ✅", "No use of unconfirmed fractals or repainting indicators: all levels (reference, protected) are derived solely from A-B OHLC and fixed buffers — static once A/B close. ✅"], "fatal": false, "non_fatal": ["No explicit out-of-sample validation or walk-forward test design provided — will be added during our own verification.", "No spread, slippage, or commission modelling in signal generation — these are handled only in optional execution gate (InpMaxSpreadPoints etc.), not in signal definition.", "No statistical justification or optimization report for thresholds (InpBreakBufferPoints=10, InpRetestTolerancePoints=30, etc.) — treated as hyperparameters to be tuned.", "Assumes aligned timeframes (e.g., D1/M1); non-aligned pairs (e.g., 